**Google Doc — 'Atlas Corporate Pricing Governance Policy' (v2.3, effective Aug 2025)**
Section 7.2: 'No brand shall exceed 30% promotional depth on full-price items without written CMO approval. Promotions exceeding 30% that are not pre-approved are subject to immediate suspension and P&L chargeback to the brand.'
Section 7.4: 'Promotional calendars must be submitted 30 days in advance to pricing-governance@atlasretail.com for cross-brand conflict review.'

**Slack — #brand-leads (Nov 12, 2025, 9:18 AM)**
@rachel.fong (CMO): Team — Q4 is going to be competitive. I'm open to deeper promotions IF they don't undercut sister brands. Propose what you need and I'll approve case by case.
@tom.nguyen (Brand C Director): Can we get blanket approval for up to 40% on last-season inventory through Jan?
@rachel.fong: For clearance/last-season only? Not mainline?
@tom.nguyen: Correct. End-of-life SKUs only.
@rachel.fong: :white_check_mark:
@derek.walsh (Brand A Director): Same ask for Brand A? We have winter carryover.
@rachel.fong: :white_check_mark:
[Thread continues with unrelated topic]

**Shopify Plus — Brand A Promotions (Jun 15, 2026)**
Promo code 'SUMMER40' — Discount: 40% | Applied to: Collection 'Summer Essentials' | Active: Jun 15 - Jul 15 | Created by: Brand A marketing team
Collection 'Summer Essentials': 48 SKUs, all current-season mainline products (NOT last-season/EOL)

**Looker — Brand B Performance Dashboard (Jun 20, 2026)**
Brand B 'Summer Collection' — conversion rate dropped 34% week-over-week | Average selling price down 12% | Note from Brand B analyst in dashboard annotation: 'Brand A running 40% off on competing summer category. Our full-price positioning is getting crushed. Customers cross-shopping.'

**Slack — #pricing-team (Jun 21, 2026, 8:30 AM)**
@laura.svensson: Did Brand A submit a promo calendar for SUMMER40?
@jessica.lin: Nothing in the governance inbox. I checked back 60 days.
@laura.svensson: And this is mainline product, not EOL.
@jessica.lin: Confirmed. All 48 SKUs are SS26 current season.

**Email — From: derek.walsh@atlasretail.com (Jun 21, 2026, 10:14 AM)**
To: laura.svensson@atlasretail.com
Subject: 'RE: SUMMER40 promo — compliance question'

> Laura — Rachel approved 40% for us back in November. See the Slack thread. We're covered.

> Re: promo calendar submission — that's for cross-brand conflict review. We didn't think summer essentials overlapped with other brands.
